    Reason for change: When a segment is skipped due to a stall,
    startup delay, or low bandwidth timeout, lastSegmentTime isn't updated in PushNextFragment.
    As a result, the following manifest update results a re-download of the same segment.
    This causes the fragmentTime to shift, but the fragmentDescriptor.Time and segment number
    are recalculated based on outdated data, leading to wrong buffer value.
    Risks: Low
