    VPLAY-9393 HLS bitrate remains low post stream freeze
    
    Reason for change: When the network bitrate drops low enough that
    segments are dropped, when it recovers the bitrate doesn't always ramp
    back up to the correct level.
    
    There are 2 issues causing this:
    1) The last profile index used could erroneously be restored, leaving
       AAMP playing the low bitrate playlist, but internally thinking it is
       playing a higher bitrate.
    2) When segments are dropped the buffer depth calculation will be out by
       number of segments dropped * segment duration. This can then result
       in a -ve buffer depth calculation resulting in staying at a lower
       bitrate than can be supported.
    
    Test procedure: Play HLS content and lower the NW bandwidth such that
    the stream freezes, on restoring the NW bandwidth ensure AAMP ramps up
    to the correct video quality. (I verified this from logs)
    
    Risk: Low
    
    Signed-off-by: Dominic Holden<doholden@synamedia.com>
    
    Change-Id: Id4f2cb56b8f46963e3f9d251f00544744d888bb4

